(j) AFMC Deputy Director', '69f754a34fa68f12b2974d4032b37e24a61b4f89841dbd13a966a3190ea7bd9f', 6, 6, '6', 25, null, null, false, null),
  ('33d4a5df-eef4-5fbe-a914-70ddfce18d3b', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'self_development', 'O-5', 'active', 'Lieutenant Colonel — Self-Development', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Lieutenant Colonels must complete DoD FM Certification Level 3. Lieutenant Colonels should strive to attain CDFM–A certification and possess a graduate or postgraduate degree or higher. Additionally, Lieutenant Colonels should seek FC functional training, including, but not limited to, Fiscal Law, GFEBS Cost Management, ABAC, ECC, DDSC, DFMC, the Discipline and Practice of Strategy Course, or Senior Resource Management Course to enhance professional development.', '3794edeaf50dd244a0ba9bfd0554426c1693dbce5cac76f1799b42e7ad74c00e', 6, 6, '6', 26, null, null, false, null),
  ('f5eda0ae-35a8-5db8-ba5e-008b8a4510f2', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'rank_duties', 'O-5', 'active', 'Lieutenant Colonel — Desired Experience', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Lieutenant Colonels must attain advanced technical and tactical skills in the application of FC core competencies and information systems, MDMP, Army doctrine (see Fig.2), and unit training management. They must gain advanced knowledge of U.S Government operations, geopolitics, DIME, PMESII-PT, ‘How the Army Runs’, JIIM, Fiscal Law, PPBE, FC core competencies, force structure, and characteristics. Lieutenant Colonels should continue institutional, operational, and self-development efforts to expand expertise in all aspects of FC to include JIIM operations.', 'cb84f9e429c93187696b854e771230be2ba79f3c9845973f623afe4f113b8fe9', 7, 7, '7', 27, null, null, false, null),
  ('a19efd45-cb05-5b7d-b104-f39599ae8d08', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'training', 'O-6', 'active', 'Colonel — Education', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Colonels must complete SSC either in a resident or non- resident capacity.', 'c12bf6ce3916393d4d4c55959780d22055fcf6d91abd2211d40ccfae9304bba1', 7, 7, '7', 28, null, null, false, null),
  ('eee94b91-81bd-5d96-82dc-a0fed70bb8cf', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-6', 'active', 'Colonel — Key Designated Billet (KDB) Positions', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', '(a) Corps G–8/Comptroller
(b) AFMC Director
(c) USASOC G–8/Comptroller
(d) USASMDC G–8/Comptroller
(e) INSCOM G–8/Comptroller
(f) EUSA G–8/Comptroller', 'b6c4034fdb2c49d4f486be0d6a0da53628b0f0f146291e21a91d7788a4ada711', 7, 7, '7', 29, null, null, false, null),
  ('6c7fd62b-fed0-5b44-8c07-695095235a4c', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-6', 'active', 'Colonel — Broadening Assignments', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'All non-KDB positions are considered broadening: “Purposeful expansion of an individual’s capabilities and understanding…that are gained through experiences in different organizational cultures and interest…” AR 600-3.
(a) ASA (FM&C) Military Deputy XO
(b) ASA (FM&C) Program Budget Officer
(c) ASA (FM&C) Executive Officer
(d) ASA (FM&C) Chief, Congressional Budget Liaison (SAM-BUL)
(e) Chief of Staff
(f) Integration Director
(g) Chief, PPBE Integration ABO
(h) ASCC/ACOM/OSD/DA/USAFMCOM Staff
(i) FC School Commandant.
(j) USAFMCOM Chief of Staff
(k) Joint Assignment
(l) Combatant Command ASCC G–8/Comptroller', '40a68ee05485691461aa761f76d5bd3919f4f731d99176ae2e497a3bad693fb4', 7, 7, '7', 30, null, null, false, null),
  ('a369e707-c19b-5920-b879-41ff1a49f0c7', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'self_development', 'O-6', 'active', 'Colonel — Self-Development', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Colonels must obtain DoD FM Certification Level 3, should obtain CDFM– A certification, and must possess a graduate or higher degree. Colonels should attend FC functional training, including, but not limited to, Fiscal Law, DDSC, SRMC, or the National Security Management Course to enhance professional development.', 'de890fc2b8ac5cd03140e2a785550884f61c4b83cb765d33d7836dd0c89014aa', 7, 7, '7', 31, null, null, false, null),
  ('77a0f4e9-e1c8-5793-9a05-076777427985', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'rank_duties', 'O-6', 'active', 'Colonel — Desired Experience', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Colonels must attain expert technical and tactical skills in the application of FC core competencies and information systems, MDMP, Army doctrine (see Fig.2), and unit training management. They must gain expert knowledge of U.S Government operations, geopolitics, DIME, PMESII-PT, ‘How the Army Runs’, JIIM, Fiscal Law, PPBE, FC core competencies, force structure, and characteristics. Colonels should continue institutional, operational, and self-development efforts to expand their knowledge at operational or strategic levels. Colonels should have joint and Army enterprise experience and have served in assignments that provide routine 3- and 4-star general officer exposure.', '3d7ace7266b6d46e79c1ac21aa1f1900c6d8c25ce863769865bbede473802380', 7, 7, '7', 32, null, null, false, null),
  ('34e1a85e-be65-5bd2-a68c-8b11b21f6041', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'warrant', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'development', 'W-1..W-5', null, 'Warrant officers', '4. Finance and Comptroller Warrant Officer Development', 'There are no warrant officers in the FC branch.', 'ef766aad895d2a8b922b788333158319f584cb6b540d8011d74f887debf477b1', 9, 9, '9', 33, null, null, false, null),
  ('a1b59b32-e6c7-5abd-8110-7d4cc0e294f2', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'development', null, 'reserve', 'Officer Development', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', 'The RC officer Finance and Comptroller (FC) lifecycle development and utilization model (Fig 3) provides general guidelines on the assignments, training, knowledge, skills, and behaviors that must contribute to a successful reserve component FC officer career.', '51ca4e2b973aaca58380e7a6db33b15746064ab62005efa944dafcb913699b28', 10, 10, '10', 34, null, null, false, null),
  ('d76cc019-70d8-5fd6-a9be-dc802f104d2c', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'training', 'O-1..O-3', 'reserve', 'Company Grade — Education', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', 'The Finance and Comptroller BOLC is the starting point for newly accessed FC officers. FC company grade officers should complete the resident BOLC by their second year of service. Army Reserve officers who have completed a BOLC other than FC BOLC can satisfy FC BOLC requirements by completing the following courses: Disbursing Operations Course, and Accounts Payable Administration Course. FC Captains must complete either the resident FC CCC or the three- phase FC CCC–RC. This course includes one distributed learning phase of nonresident instruction; and two active duty for training phases at the Finance and Comptroller School. AGRs will attend the six- month resident course unless an exception is made by HQDA. Officers who have completed CCC in a different branch must have a minimum of two years in a FC key development or utilization assignment, or complete the Defense Comptrollership Program to satisfy CCC requirements. Additionally, these officers must complete the following ATIS courses: the Disbursing Operations Course, the Accounts Payable Administration Course; and the following ATRRS courses: GFEBS Cost Management and Army PPBE.', 'd297d4462e8225bcc832b4924e61904a43c73c477a8f9c4a537beddbbab1ee27', 10, 10, '10', 35, null, null, false, null),
  ('31e4486a-bac2-5f9a-b261-d36bdf0752f3', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-1..O-3', 'reserve', 'Company Grade — Key Developmental Assignments (see Fig 3)', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', '(a) Finance Company Commander
(b) Brigade S-8
(c) Company Commander (90A/01A)
(d) Disbursing Officer', '065072156527a1acc39777dc76c72f9bfd5fc86ba71fd35b101fb338b13b06a5', 10, 10, '10', 36, null, null, false, null),
  ('97e89cfc-4738-599e-89c9-44c52686a594', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-1..O-3', 'reserve', 'Company Grade — Broadening assignments (see Fig 3)', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', '(a) MSC/Budget Officer
(b) FIBN Staff
(c) FISC Plans and Operations Officer (CUOPS)', '589b93616e2215a41a17894be6fd772272916b478270099eefcb46d25813bd1c', 10, 10, '10', 37, null, null, false, null),
  ('ad51840a-1210-5f23-addb-9d5e4e9b5a30', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'self_development', 'O-1..O-3', 'reserve', 'Company Grade — Additional Training/Self Development', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', 'Company grade officers must obtain and maintain their mandated DoD Financial Management program certification at Level I or Level II accordingly. Additionally, company grade officers should strive for a professional credential. Examples include CDFM, Certified Government Financial Manager (CGFM), Certified Government Auditing Professional (CGAP), or Certified Public Finance Officer (CPFO). Reserve Component company grade officers should also seek additional Financial Management functional training to ensure they are well-rounded. See Figure 1 for recommended functional training.', '1484c3b1fe3eb53f862b90efe9663812c5b5a1b59898ddcb2e9250013d883657', 10, 10, '10', 38, null, null, false, null),
  ('77378b40-ccab-56cd-83a2-14b900a103f3', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'rank_duties', 'O-1..O-3', 'reserve', 'Company Grade — Desired Experience', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', 'Company grade officers are placed in assignments where they have fiduciary responsibility and pecuniary liability for public funds entrusted to them. They must be proficient in FC technical financial systems and disbursing operations.', 'f61497427b61b7529c01df9233e992244852b3cced0eb8c1edff9d5761274053', 10, 10, '10', 39, null, null, false, null),
  ('7d8d38bc-c10a-511f-9202-ba094d3bf99b', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'training', 'O-4..O-6', 'reserve', 'Field Grade — Education', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', 'FC majors must complete the ILE common core curriculum for promotion to lieutenant colonel. Lieutenant colonels must complete either the legacy Command and General Staff Officer Course, or the ILE Common Core curriculum and ILE Advanced Operations and Warfighting Course to be considered for SSC. SSC completion is highly recommended for promotion to colonel. Field grade officers who have completed CCC in a different branch are required to have at least two years of experience in a FC key development or utilization assignment, or completion of the Defense Comptrollership Program to be considered for promotion to LTC. These officers must also complete the following ATIS courses: Disbursing Operations Course, Accounts Payable Administration Course. Additionally, they must complete the following ATRRS courses: GFEBS Cost Management and Army PPBE.', 'aeb944fa15d31e74084c51cdc8c23ac7dfa032cdf0dcbcba4d3182e21efec5d5', 10, 10, '10', 40, null, null, false, null),
  ('78fbab4e-767c-53de-9847-46f4147400ef', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-4', 'reserve', 'Field Grade — Key Developmental assignments for majors (see Fig 3)', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', '(a) 2-Star Command Budget Officer
(b) ESC G-8/Comptroller
(c) Division Deputy G8
(d) Disbursing Officer
(e) FISC Branch Chief
